     "page": 1,
     "text": "**Green LLC Clinic**\n\nRe: Elizabeth Rios (DOB 02/12/1981)\n\n---\n\n**May 24, 2025**\n\nMs. Elizabeth Rios, a 44-year-old female, presented today for her annual flu shot. Her blood pressure was measured at 143/73 mmHg, and her weight was 150 pounds. Upon examination, she appeared to be in good health with no acute distress. She is currently taking atomoxetine 40 mg for her ADHD, which is well-controlled. She reports that her symptoms have been effectively managed, and she has been adhering to her medication regimen. She mentioned experiencing some mild, routine insomnia but no other significant complaints. We discussed general wellness and preventive care for the upcoming flu season. \n\n---\n\n**August 21, 2024**\n\nMs. Elizabeth Rios returned today for a follow-up regarding her ADHD. Her blood pressure was 146/85 mmHg, and she weighed 156 pounds. She reports feeling generally well and her ADHD symptoms remain controlled. Her atomoxetine 40 mg has been effective, and she continues to experience minimal side effects. She has been engaging cognitive-behavioral therapy which has been beneficial. During the visit, she mentioned mild seasonal allergies but nothing has affected her overall health. The physical examination was unremarkable aside from some mild erythema on her hands which she attributes to dry weather. \n\n---\n\n**November 18, 2023**\n\nOn this visit, Elizabeth Rios came in to discuss her ADHD management. Her blood pressure was 146/83 mmHg, and her weight was 149 pounds. Ms. Rios is currently taking atomoxetine 40 mg which is helping her manage her ADHD effectively. She has not reported any side from the medication and her symptoms remain well-controlled. She noted mild fatigue but attributed it to a recent upper respiratory infection. routine physical examination revealed no significant abnormalities. She has been attending regular sessions of cognitive-behavioral therapy, which have been aiding in her overall mental well-being.\n\n---\n\n**February 14, 2023**\n\nMs. Elizabeth Rios visited today for a follow-up regarding her ADHD, which has been diagnosed since 2017. Her blood pressure was 140/85 mmHg, and her weight was 155 pounds. She is currently taking atomoxetine 40 mg daily for her ADHD, which is well-controlled. She reports feeling well and has been to her treatment plan without any issues. She has been attending her scheduled sessions of cognitive-behavioral therapy, which have been helpful. She has mild occasional headaches but attributes them to stress from work. The rest of her physical examination was unremarkable.\n\n---\n\n**"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "Social History:**\n\nMs. Rios reports that she used to smoke cigarettes but quit in May 2016. She used to smoke one pack per day and was honest about smoking history. Currently, she consumes approximately six alcoholic drinks per week. She has a family history of COPD in her mother, who was diagnosed at age 71 and is currently 43 years old and doing well.\n\n---\n\n**Summary:**\n\nMs. Elizabeth Rios been under consistent care for her ADHD, which is well-managed with atomoxetine 40 mg. blood pressure and weight have been within normal limits during her visits. She has a history of former tobacco use and moderate alcohol consumption. Her overall health appears to be stable with no significant acute issues.\n\n**Dr. Gregory White** \nGreen LLC Clinic \nSpecialty: Psychiatry\n"
